John Richert wrote:
> What are the easier classes to ascend with?  So far, it seems like Valkyries 
> and Knights have been the easiest.  For whatever reason, I seem to have 
> trouble with Samurais.  Any other suggested classes? 

I'd say valkyrie, barbarian, priest and wizard.

The priest's ability to see the cursed/blessed status of items without 
identifying them is just awesome, and also starting with holy water is 
great. Priests also randomly have a magic marker, and they have 
near-mandatory-for-ascension starting spells at times (remove curse and 
identify). Their quest item is ok, too.

Wizards start out with such a load of stuff and have such an easy time 
with spells. Guaranteed great starting items are a cloak of magic 
resistance and the spell of force bolt, which'll both benefit you 
greatly especially since you won't really be running out of MP with a 
wizard. Also, the 33% of being able to write unknown scrolls and 
spellbooks is a nice bonus. Don't have to wish for those scrolls of 
genocide and charging anymore, just wish for magic markers and give it a 
couple of tries =)

Valks have a far better quest item than barbarians, but barbs come with 
poison resistance. When you're new to the game, your biggest problems 
include knowing what (not) to eat..thus a barbarian must be the easiest 
class to start out with. However, I find that identifying stuff with 
fighters such as v and b and is a pain as you don't start out with any 
magic items (identifying magic, holy water, magic markers) and you'll 
generally have to do it the hard way (=just try reading/quaffing them).

Samurai are a crap version of valkyries. Always lawful, awful quest item 
etc. Decent armor, but that's easy to get from the mines anyway. Good 
weapon skills, but that's it. Stick with valkyries, I'd say.

Out of my 10 or so ascensions, most have been valks and priests. None 
have been monks, tourists, rogues or healers..so avoid them. They're 
crap and mostly there for the challenge. Healers have a great quest 
artifact but any neutral character can wish for it, healers can't (can't 
wish for your own quest artifact) so don't play them either until you 
know your NH.


